"Let $G$ be an undirected graph, and let $F_1,F_2,\\ldots,F_n$ be sets of edges in $G$. For a family of edge sets, let $rg(F_1,\\ldots,F_n)$ denote the length of its shortest rainbow cycle. **Rainbow Caccetta–Häggkvist conjecture.** If each $F_i$ has size at most $k$, then\n\n$$\nrg(F_1,F_2,\\ldots,F_n)\\leq \\big\\lceil \\frac{n}{k}\\big\\rceil.\n$$\n\nThis is a rainbow analogue of the Caccetta–Häggkvist conjecture, relating prescribed edge colours to short rainbow cycles. The paper presents it as a conjecture suggested by the first author; the stated general form remains open."